  "id": "cap-0034/tx-too-late-with-fee-charged",
  "title": "txTOO_LATE in a closed ledger (Protocol 13): fee charged, sequence number not consumed, no operation applied",
  "kind": "ledger",
  "caps": [
    34
  ],
  "protocol": {
    "introduced": 1
  },
  "synthetic": false,
  "negative": false,
  "validity": "valid",
  "shapes": [
    "tx-too-late",
    "failed-tx-fee-charged",
    "sequence-not-bumped",
    "time-bounds-max-time",
    "pre-protocol-15-close-time-race"
  ],
  "why": "Before Protocol 15 (CAP-34) a transaction was checked against the previous ledger's close time when it was nominated and against the new close time when it was applied, so one whose max_time fell between the two was included, charged its fee and then failed with txTOO_LATE without consuming its sequence number. Here max_time is one second before the ledger's close time. Readers that assume a failed transaction always bumps the source's sequence number, that expect operation results on every failed transaction, or that treat txTOO_LATE as a submission error that never reaches a ledger get this transaction wrong.",
  "fields": {
